From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wenziwanka <tech@wenziwanka.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 12:40:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: hci_sync: do not fail init when the controller rejects the default link policy

hci_setup_link_policy_sync() builds the default link policy from the
controller's LMP features and fails hci_dev_open() if the controller
rejects it. The Unisoc UWE5623 (Marlin3E) advertises Park state but
answers Write Default Link Policy Settings including HCI_LP_PARK with
Invalid HCI Command Parameters (0x12), so the adapter never comes up:

  Bluetooth: hci0: Opcode 0x080f failed: -22

A default link policy is a convenience, not a requirement. When the
controller rejects it with Invalid Parameters, retry without Park and,
should that be rejected too, keep whatever default the controller has
instead of failing the whole initialization.

Signed-off-by: wenziwanka <tech@wenziwanka.com>
---

--- a/net/bluetooth/hci_sync.c
+++ b/net/bluetooth/hci_sync.c
@@ -4326,6 +4326,7 @@
 {
 	struct hci_cp_write_def_link_policy cp;
 	u16 link_policy = 0;
+	int err;
 
 	if (!(hdev->commands[5] & 0x10))
 		return 0;
@@ -4343,8 +4344,30 @@
 
 	cp.policy = cpu_to_le16(link_policy);
 
-	return __hci_cmd_sync_status(hdev, HCI_OP_WRITE_DEF_LINK_POLICY,
-				     sizeof(cp), &cp, HCI_CMD_TIMEOUT);
+	err = __hci_cmd_sync_status(hdev, HCI_OP_WRITE_DEF_LINK_POLICY,
+				    sizeof(cp), &cp, HCI_CMD_TIMEOUT);
+	if (err != -EINVAL)
+		return err;
+
+	/* Some controllers advertise Park state in their LMP features but
+	 * answer Write Default Link Policy Settings with Invalid HCI Command
+	 * Parameters when it is included (seen on the Unisoc UWE5623). A
+	 * default link policy is not worth failing the whole init for:
+	 * retry without Park, and if even that is rejected carry on with
+	 * whatever default the controller has.
+	 */
+	if (link_policy & HCI_LP_PARK) {
+		bt_dev_warn(hdev, "Controller rejected Park in default link policy, retrying without it");
+		cp.policy = cpu_to_le16(link_policy & ~HCI_LP_PARK);
+		err = __hci_cmd_sync_status(hdev, HCI_OP_WRITE_DEF_LINK_POLICY,
+					    sizeof(cp), &cp, HCI_CMD_TIMEOUT);
+		if (err != -EINVAL)
+			return err;
+	}
+
+	bt_dev_warn(hdev, "Controller rejected default link policy 0x%4.4x, ignoring",
+		    link_policy);
+	return 0;
 }
 
 static int hci_read_page_scan_activity_sync(struct hci_dev *hdev)
